<v Richard Castellano>Did you read about me? Oh yes I did. No, you didn't. Well, I didn't even get the paper today. You know, that's Billy Crystal.
<v Richard Castellano>你在报纸上读到过我吗？哦，是的，我读过。不，你没有。嗯，我今天甚至都没拿到报纸。你知道，那是比利·克里斯托。

00:24:21.050 --> 00:24:34.910
<v Alex Blumberg>Castellano acted out whole stretches of dialogue from scenes in which he didn't even appear, like someone who'd watched the film dozens of times. It wasn't hard for him to package the dream of Hollywood to the people of Narrowsburg. It was a dream he understood.
<v Alex Blumberg>卡斯特拉诺演出了整段整段他甚至没有出场的电影对话，就像一个把电影看了几十遍的人。对他来说，向纳罗斯堡的人兜售好莱坞梦想并不难。这是一个他自己也深陷其中的梦想。

00:24:34.910 --> 00:25:13.510
<v Richard Castellano>Well, I know the feeling it gave me, that I'd go to sleep every night still thinking, did I really act with De Niro in that? I mean, you read, hear so much about big celebrity, the guy that made hundreds of movies. All this talk of the world, he's the best actor in the world. Then here you are, standing right with him, shaking his hand, drinking coffee with him, acting across from him, walking with him and, you know, just being involved with him. It's the most exciting-- the next exciting feeling I'll ever get is when I meet God. That'll be the closest I can get to how I felt when I met Bobby De Niro.
<v Richard Castellano>嗯，我知道那种感觉，我每天晚上睡觉时还在想，我真的和德尼罗演过戏吗？我的意思是，你读到、听到那么多关于大明星的消息，那个拍了几百部电影的人。全世界都在谈论他，他是世界上最好的演员。然后你就在这儿，和他站在一起，和他握手，和他喝咖啡，和他演对手戏，和他一起走，你知道，仅仅是参与其中。这是最令人兴奋的……我下一次能得到的最兴奋的感觉就是见到上帝的时候。那将是我能感受到的、最接近我见到鲍比·德尼罗时感觉的东西了。

00:25:13.510 --> 00:25:34.000
<v Alex Blumberg>Everyone I spoke with in Narrowsburg got asked the same question-- if all this were made into a movie, who would you want to play the part of you? And all of them said the same thing, from John Borg, to Zac Pontier, to Richie Castellano. They wanted to play themselves.
<v Alex Blumberg>我在纳罗斯堡采访的每个人都被问到了同一个问题——如果这一切被拍成电影，你想让谁来演你？他们都说了同样的话，从约翰·博格到扎克·庞蒂尔，再到里奇·卡斯特拉诺。他们都想演自己。

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:45.790
<v Ira Glass>Alex Blumberg is a producer here at This American Life . Four Deadly Reasons was finally released in 2002, and that's two years after this story first was broadcast. It played a few festivals and then went to DVD.
<v Ira Glass>亚历克斯·布隆伯格是我们《美国生活》的制作人。《四个致命理由》最终在2002年上映，那是这个故事首次播出两年后。它在几个电影节上放映过，然后出了DVD。

